    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0423" n="1213" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v01p2/pg1213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">460.509/6–1854</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of Foreign Operations (Stassen) to the President of the Board of Trade
                        of the United Kingdom (Thorneycroft)</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d115-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-06-18">June 18, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You will recall that in my last message to you,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d115-f2"/>
                    and in reply to your proposal that currently agreed items should be decontrolled
                    approximately 20 June, I stated for given reasons I had to reserve my
                    position.</p>
                <p>Since the next two weeks may be the crucial period in the Hanoi Delta, and the
                    further period is unpredictable, I should like to advise you that until the
                    situation with respect to Indo-China becomes more clear, I must withhold my
                    concurrence to the decontrol of items agreed for deletion.</p>
                <p>I trust that your appraisal of the seriousness of that situation has led you to
                    the same conclusion.</p>
                <p>I am sending a copy of this message to M. Schumann.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d115-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d115-f1-content">
                <p>This message was transmitted in telegram 6958 to London, June 18, 1954.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d115-f2" n="2" xml:id="d115-f2-content">
                <p>Dated June 5, <ref target="#pg1176">p. 1176</ref>.</p>
            </note>
